course: dictionary
lesson: 15920
title: Unplanned
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unplanned means not planned or expected. It happened without being arranged first. The prefix un- often means "not", so unplanned is the opposite of planned.
explain: «The bus broke down, so the class had an unplanned stop at a park.» Nobody arranged the stop. The clues are broke down and so, which show it was a surprise. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then test your meaning in the sentence.
explain: In maths, an unplanned cost changes the total. «The family had unplanned costs when the car needed a new tyre.» They did not budget for the tyre, so their money went further than they expected.
fact: Unplanned means not planned or expected.
fact: The prefix un- often means "not", so unplanned is the opposite of planned.
fact: «Unplanned» can describe a stop, a trip, a cost or a party.
fact: «Completely unplanned» means that nothing at all was arranged beforehand.
fact: Planning for the unplanned, such as keeping a first aid kit or a phone, is a wise way to get ready for surprises.
exercise: «The bus broke down, so the class had an unplanned stop at a park.» What does unplanned mean here? | Noisy and fun | *Not arranged or expected beforehand | Very long and tiring | Planned for weeks in advance
exercise: «The family had unplanned costs when the car needed a new tyre.» What does unplanned mean here? | Cheap and easy to fix | *Not budgeted for, so they had not expected to pay it | Paid for on purpose, as a treat | Very large and very old
exercise: Which word means the opposite of unplanned? | *Planned | Hurried | Careless | Muddy
test: «The party was completely unplanned, but everyone still had fun.» What does completely unplanned mean? | Very loud and busy | Held outside in the rain | Carefully arranged down to the last detail | *Nothing was arranged before it started
test: Mum keeps a first aid kit in the car. Why is this wise? | Because first aid kits are heavy and fun to carry | *Because accidents can be unplanned, so it is good to be ready | Because the kit makes the car go faster | Because the kit is always needed on a planned picnic
exam: Which sentence uses unplanned correctly? | The trip was unplanned because we booked every hotel a year ago | The lesson was unplanned because the teacher had written every step in advance | The dinner was unplanned because the menu was printed on cards | *The sudden storm was unplanned, and nobody had prepared for it
